  "description_text": "Printed plastic threads can wear out or strip over time, especially in parts that are assembled and disassembled repeatedly. Brass heat-set inserts provide durable metal threads, helping improve assembly strength and making printed parts more suitable for repeated fastening.\n\nThe included heat-insert tooling supports common insert sizes used in 3D printing, including M2, M2.5, M3, M4, M5, M6, and M8. This makes it easier to handle a wide range of printed enclosures, brackets, and functional assemblies.\n\nThe included adapter is designed for 900M / T18-style removable-tip soldering irons. Other soldering iron systems may require a different adapter.\n\nHakko FX-888D / FX-888, T18-style irons Fits? Yes Notes Included adapter replaces the standard removable tip Hakko 936 / 937 / 907 handle Fits? Yes Notes 900M-style tip interface 936-style stations (Yihua, Baku, Kaisi, Aoyue, Vastar, etc.) Fits? Yes Notes Compatible if the iron uses 900M-style removable tips Generic adjustable iron using 900M tips Fits? Yes Notes 60 W or higher recommended TS100 / TS101 / SQ-001 / Pinecil V1 Fits? No — different adapter required Notes Needs a TS100-style shank; not included Pinecil V2 Fits? No Notes Different tip interface; TS100 adapters do not fit T12 / T15 cartridge irons Fits? No Notes Cartridge heater — this set cannot attach JBC C245 / C210, Aixun, Sugon, Sequre, FNIRSI HS-02A Fits? No Notes Cartridge irons; also a different thread than this kit Weller ET / LT / XT Fits? No Notes Proprietary tip series ERSA 102 / 832 / 842 Fits? No Notes Proprietary tip series Butane or fixed-tip irons Fits? No Notes Tip must be removable\n\nHakko FX-888D / FX-888, T18-style irons Fits? Yes Notes Included adapter replaces the standard removable tip\n\nHakko FX-888D / FX-888, T18-style irons\n\nFits? Yes\n\nFits?\n\nYes\n\nNotes Included adapter replaces the standard removable tip\n\nNotes\n\nIncluded adapter replaces the standard removable tip\n\nHakko 936 / 937 / 907 ha